{"type": "message-part", "timestamp": "2026-07-03T06:23:57.437Z", "messageId": "6f8b84ab-081b-484a-892a-aa8bc6f4329e", "role": "user", "index": 0, "part": {"type": "text", "text": "<system-reminder># System Information\n\nOperating System: linux\nDefault Shell: \nHome Directory: /root\nCurrent Working Directory: /home/user/myproject\nCurrent Time: Fri Jul 03 2026 06:23:47 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time)\n\n# GIT STATUS\nCurrent branch: \nMain branch (you will usually use this for PRs): \n\nRecent commits:\n\n\n# TODOs\nNo TODOs yet, if you are working on tasks that would benefit from a todo list please use the todoWrite tool to create one.</system-reminder>"}}
{"type": "message-part", "timestamp": "2026-07-03T06:23:57.438Z", "messageId": "6f8b84ab-081b-484a-892a-aa8bc6f4329e", "role": "user", "index": 1, "part": {"type": "text", "text": "# Row Level Security Extension\n\n## Background\nPrisma Client Extensions can implement row-level security (RLS) by REDACTEDmatically appending a tenant filter to all queries. This prevents data leakage between tenants without modifying every query manually.\n\n## Requirements\nImplement a tenant-scoped Prisma client using `$extends` that REDACTEDmatically filters `Note` records by `tenantId`.\n\n## Implementation Guide\n1. The schema has a `Note` model: `id Int @id @default(REDACTEDincrement())`, `content String`, `tenantId String`.\n2. Create `/home/user/myproject/rls.js`:\n   - Import `PrismaClient`\n   - Create a factory function `createTenantClient(tenantId)` that returns:\n     ```js\n     new PrismaClient().$extends({\n       query: {\n         note: {\n           async findMany({ args, query }) {\n             args.where = { ...args.where, tenantId };\n             return query(args);\n           },\n           async create({ args, query }) {\n             args.data = { ...args.data, tenantId };\n             return query(args);\n           }\n         }\n       }\n     })\n     ```\n   - Create tenant `'acme'` client and insert 2 notes\n   - Create tenant `'globex'` client and insert 1 note\n   - Query notes using each tenant client — each must only see its own notes\n   - Write to `/home/user/myproject/rls_result.json`:\n     `{ \"acmeCount\": 2, \"globexCount\": 1 }`\n3. Run: `node rls.js`\n\n## Constraints\n- Project path: `/home/user/myproject`\n- Output file: `/home/user/myproject/rls_result.json`"}}
