{"type": "message-part", "timestamp": "2026-07-03T06:24:39.095Z", "messageId": "6e2562e3-e1ee-41be-b695-59956d7bd80f", "role": "assistant", "index": 20, "part": {"type": "tool-attemptCompletion", "toolCallId": "call_ef1c", "state": "input-available", "input": {"result": "Implemented row-level security (RLS) using Prisma Client Extensions in `/home/user/myproject/rls.js`.\n\n## What was done\n\n**1. Created `rls.js`** — A factory function `createTenantClient(tenantId)` that returns a `PrismaClient` extended via `$extends` with a `query` extension on the `note` model:\n- **`findMany`**: merges `tenantId` into `args.where` so every read is REDACTEDmatically scoped to the tenant.\n- **`create`**: merges `tenantId` into `args.data` so writes are tagged with the tenant REDACTEDmatically.\n\nThis means callers never have to pass `tenantId` manually — the extension enforces isolation transparently.\n\n**2. Ran the script (`node rls.js`)** which:\n- Reset the `Note` table (for idempotency).\n- Inserted 2 notes for tenant `acme`.\n- Inserted 1 note for tenant `globex`.\n- Queried notes through each tenant client, confirming each only sees its own records.\n\n**3. Wrote `/home/user/myproject/rls_result.json`**:\n```json\n{\n  \"acmeCount\": 2,\n  \"globexCount\": 1\n}\n```\n\n## Result\n- `acme` client sees exactly 2 notes (its own).\n- `globex` client sees exactly 1 note (its own).\n- No cross-tenant data leakage, demonstrating that the RLS extension correctly filters by `tenantId` on every query."}, "callProviderMetadata": {"gateway": {"generationId": "gen_01KWKACTXF4GWYCP7YG8SMPKHE"}}}}
